1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
That ticking sound

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
when you start your car cold?

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,500
Loudest right after startup.

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,000
Quiets down in a minute or two.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,500
One clue: a small exhaust manifold leak.

6
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,000
Metal contracts when cold, so the gap ticks until it seals up warm.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
That gap can also let exhaust gas —

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
including carbon monoxide — into the engine bay.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,500
Don't ignore a cold-start tick.

10
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,000
A quick listen can confirm where it's coming from.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Worth checking before it gets worse.

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Stop by and we'll take a look — Nick's Tire & Auto.
